#* {{quote-book|en|date=October 23, 1544| title=Letters |author=Lord Evre |  passage=''Thomas Carlysle'', &c. rode a Forrey to ''Dunglas'', and there seased and brought away 80 Nolt, 200 Shepe, 22 Naggs. A '''Rode''' made to a Stede called the ''Hayrebed'', and there they gate 30 Nolt, 3 or 4 Naggs.}}
#* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|year=1596.2|book=VI|stanza=8|page=461|passage=There dwelt a ſaluage nation, which did liue / Of ſtealth and ſpoile, and making nightly '''rode''' / Into their neighbours borders{{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|book=1 Samuel|chapter=27|verse=10|column=1|passage=And Achiſh said, Whither haue ye made a '''rode''' to day? And Dauid said, Againſt the South of Iudah, and againſt the South of the Ierahmeelites, and againſt the South of the Kenites.}}

